From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 13:50:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] do not apply a regulatory domain from the notifier

wiphy_apply_custom_regulatory() takes rtnl_lock(), and cfg80211 calls
reg_notifier with it held: `iw reg set US` deadlocks rtnl, and every
netlink user with it, sshd included.

The call belongs before wiphy registration, where cfg80211_regd_set_wiphy()
already makes it. Drop it from the notifier and keep the channel parsing
the firmware needs. Measured: `iw reg set US` returns 0, the domain becomes
DFS-FCC, and 2.4 GHz still associates in 2 s.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
--- a/wlan/os/linux/gl_cfg80211.c
+++ b/wlan/os/linux/gl_cfg80211.c
@@ -3493,7 +3493,13 @@ DOMAIN_SEND_CMD:
 		}
 
 
-		mtk_apply_custom_regulatory(pWiphy, pRegdom);
+		/* wiphy_apply_custom_regulatory() takes rtnl_lock(), and
+		 * cfg80211 calls this notifier holding it. Applying the domain
+		 * here deadlocks the thread against a lock it already owns and
+		 * strands the machine. The documented place is before
+		 * wiphy_register(), which cfg80211_regd_set_wiphy() already
+		 * does; only the channel parsing below belongs here.
+		 */
 	}
 
 
